    "numbers.py": "def total(values):\n    \"\"\"Return the sum of all non-None values in the iterable.\n\n    None values are ignored, zeros and negative numbers are included.\n    An empty input (or one that becomes empty after removing None)\n    returns 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    return sum(v for v in values if v is not None)\n",
    "labels.py": "def normalize(value):\n    \"\"\"Normalize a label by trimming outer whitespace and lowercasing.\n\n    Internal whitespace is preserved.\n    \"\"\"\n    return value.strip().lower()\n",
    "README.md": "# Helpers\n\nUtilities.\n\n## numbers.total\n\n`numbers.total(values)` returns the sum of all non-`None` values in an iterable of numbers.\n\n- `None` values are ignored.\n- Zero and negative numbers are included in the sum.\n- An empty iterable, or one that only contains `None`, returns `0`.\n\nExamples:\n\n```python\nfrom numbers import total\n\ntotal([2, None, -1, 0])  # 1\ntotal([None])            # 0\ntotal([])                # 0\n```\n\n## labels.normalize\n\n`labels.normalize(value)` normalizes a string label by:\n\n- removing leading and trailing whitespace\n- converting all characters to lowercase\n- preserving internal spaces\n\nExamples:\n\n```python\nfrom labels import normalize\n\nnormalize(' A B ')  # 'a b'\nnormalize('  ')     # ''\n```\n",
    "test_numbers.py": "import unittest\nfrom numbers import total\n\nclass NumbersTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_total(self):\n        self.assertEqual(total([2, None, -1, 0]), 1)\n    def test_empty(self):\n        self.assertEqual(total([None]), 0)\n",
    "test_labels.py": "import unittest\nfrom labels import normalize\n\nclass LabelsTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_normalize(self):\n        self.assertEqual(normalize(' A B '), 'a b')\n    def test_empty(self):\n        self.assertEqual(normalize('  '), '')\n"
